CORE
exact.c
--unwind 30 --unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ assertion r == 3: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
^\[main\.assertion\.[1-5]\] .*: FAILURE$
unwinding assertion loop \d+: FAILURE
--
The integer conversions, %c, %s and %% produce exact output: the length
returned is that of the whole output, and the buffer holds as much as fits.
Before, the output was unknown characters.
